{"page":"REV3L","gene":"REV3L","accession":"O60673","protein":"DNA polymerase zeta catalytic subunit","length":3130,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"O60673-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000368802.8","ENST00000358835.7"],"refseq":["NM_001372078.1","NM_002912.5"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001359007.1","NP_002903.3"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":null},"features":[{"type":"Modified residue","start":1030,"end":1030,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1041,"end":1041,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1724,"end":1724,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":1847,"end":1898,"description":"Mediates interaction with MAD2L2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":1967,"end":1967,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3042,"end":3042,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Zinc finger","start":3042,"end":3057,"description":"CysA-type"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3045,"end":3045,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3054,"end":3054,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3057,"end":3057,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3086,"end":3086,"description":"[4Fe-4S] cluster"},{"type":"Motif","start":3086,"end":3104,"description":"CysB motif"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3089,"end":3089,"description":"[4Fe-4S] cluster"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3099,"end":3099,"description":"[4Fe-4S] cluster"},{"type":"Binding site","start":3104,"end":3104,"description":"[4Fe-4S] cluster"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Heterodimer with MAD2L2. This dimer forms the minimal DNA polymerase zeta complex (Pol-zeta2), with REV3L bearing DNA polymerase catalytic activity, although its activity is very low in this context. Component of the tetrameric Pol-zeta complex (Pol-zeta4), which consists of REV3L, MAD2L2, POLD2 and POLD3; Pol-zeta4 i